    <contentBlocks>
      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000012",
      "key": "4997312f-0312-43b1-9b18-1c05dd8d045b",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "In this article"
        },
        {
          "alias": "linksHtml",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<ol>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"trend-1\" data-no=\"01\">Denial prevention</button></li>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"trend-2\" data-no=\"02\">Clean claim rate</button></li>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"trend-3\" data-no=\"03\">Prior authorization</button></li>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"trend-4\" data-no=\"04\">Payer automation</button></li>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"trend-5\" data-no=\"05\">Staffing squeeze</button></li>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"trend-6\" data-no=\"06\">AI ROI gap</button></li>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"trend-7\" data-no=\"07\">Outsourcing capacity</button></li>\n  <li><button type=\"button\" data-target=\"faq\" data-no=\"FAQ\">Questions answered</button></li>\n</ol>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "9803fd79-3b28-4b01-8028-5ccb31179bfc",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<div class=\"rcm-intro\">\n<p>Somewhere in your practice right now, a claim is sitting in a work queue that would have been paid without a second look two years ago.</p>\n<p>That’s the shortest possible summary of healthcare revenue cycle management trends in 2026.</p>\n<p>Denial rates are climbing, billing teams are thinner, and the technology that was supposed to absorb the difference is still not showing results for most organizations.</p>\n<p>Below are the seven trends actually reshaping revenue cycle operations this year, what the data says about each, and what it means for a physician practice, clinic, or hospital billing team.</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "ea8d089e-d2b5-449e-b38b-6cf2f2f44ead",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<section class=\"rcm-at-glance\" aria-labelledby=\"glance-title\">\n  <span class=\"rcm-section-label\" id=\"glance-title\">Seven trends at a glance</span>\n  <div class=\"rcm-trend-grid\">\n    <a class=\"rcm-trend-link\" href=\"#trend-1\"><span class=\"rcm-trend-no\">01</span><span><b>Denial prevention replaces denial cleanup</b><small>Denial rates past benchmark, appeals unaffordable</small></span></a>\n    <a class=\"rcm-trend-link\" href=\"#trend-2\"><span class=\"rcm-trend-no\">02</span><span><b>Clean claim rate becomes the headline metric</b><small>Leading indicator instead of lagging</small></span></a>\n    <a class=\"rcm-trend-link\" href=\"#trend-3\"><span class=\"rcm-trend-no\">03</span><span><b>Prior authorization automation accelerates</b><small>CMS-0057-F API deadline lands January 2027</small></span></a>\n    <a class=\"rcm-trend-link\" href=\"#trend-4\"><span class=\"rcm-trend-no\">04</span><span><b>Payer automation outpaces manual claim work</b><small>Machines review claims, people fix rejections</small></span></a>\n    <a class=\"rcm-trend-link\" href=\"#trend-5\"><span class=\"rcm-trend-no\">05</span><span><b>The staffing squeeze becomes structural</b><small>More denials, same number of people</small></span></a>\n    <a class=\"rcm-trend-link\" href=\"#trend-6\"><span class=\"rcm-trend-no\">06</span><span><b>The AI ROI gap gets named out loud</b><small>Broad adoption, narrow proven return</small></span></a>\n    <a class=\"rcm-trend-link\" href=\"#trend-7\"><span class=\"rcm-trend-no\">07</span><span><b>Outsourcing becomes a hiring workaround</b><small>Trained staff without the recruiting cycle</small></span></a>\n  </div>\n</section>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000005",
      "key": "fb32a5f0-3679-42cb-b16b-156a30b2f32b",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "number",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "01"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Denial Prevention Is Replacing Denial Cleanup"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "trend-1"
        },
        {
          "alias": "body",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>Every practice knows the 5% to 10% denial benchmark. Far fewer are hitting it.</p>\n<p>That range is <a href=\"https://www.hfma.org/revenue-cycle/kpis/7-kpis-providers-should-be-tracking/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HFMA’s published KPI standard</a>, with under 5% considered optimal. Denials have been climbing past it for years: <a href=\"https://www.experian.com/blogs/healthcare/state-of-claims-2025/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Experian Health</a> found 41% of providers now report rates of 10% or higher, up from 38% in 2024 and 30% in 2022.</p>\n<figure class=\"rcm-chart reveal-chart\" aria-labelledby=\"denial-caption\">\n  <div class=\"rcm-chart-head\"><figcaption id=\"denial-caption\"><h3>Providers reporting denial rates above 10%</h3><span class=\"rcm-chart-source\">Source: Experian Health, State of Claims</span></figcaption><span class=\"rcm-chart-note\">Select a bar</span></div>\n  <div class=\"denial-chart\">\n    <div class=\"denial-axis\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span>45%</span><span>30%</span><span>15%</span><span>0%</span></div>\n    <div class=\"denial-plot\">\n      <button class=\"denial-bar\" style=\"--h:66.67%;--bar:#8bbce8\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"2022: 30 percent\"><strong>30%</strong><span>2022</span></button>\n      <button class=\"denial-bar\" style=\"--h:84.44%;--bar:#3f91db\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"2024: 38 percent\"><strong>38%</strong><span>2024</span></button>\n      <button class=\"denial-bar\" style=\"--h:91.11%;--bar:#2369a8\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"2025: 41 percent\"><strong>41%</strong><span>2025</span></button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</figure>\n<p>For most of that period, the response was to appeal harder. That’s what has changed. Reworking a denial costs real staff hours, and denial volume has grown faster than billing headcount. The claims that lose the triage fight are never resubmitted at all.</p>\n<p>Practice leaders now name denials and appeals their single biggest source of revenue cycle leakage in <a href=\"https://www.mgma.com/mgma-stat/detecting-and-fixing-leaks-across-the-revenue-cycle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MGMA’s January 2026 Stat poll</a>, ahead of front-end issues, billing, and coding.</p>\n<p>That’s why denial management is moving upstream: real-time eligibility at registration, authorization status tied to scheduling, and root-cause categorization by payer so the same denial doesn’t recur every week.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000006",
      "key": "397fcc31-dc0a-42a6-9049-d7060cd07559",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "label",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What it means for you"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "If your team reports how many appeals it filed but not how many denials it prevented, you are measuring the wrong end of the process. Appeals cost staff hours. Prevention costs a process change."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000005",
      "key": "ae778e98-b516-4893-8560-f24087cc334a",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "number",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "02"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Clean Claim Rate Is Becoming the Headline Metric"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "trend-2"
        },
        {
          "alias": "body",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>Revenue cycle teams are shifting their primary KPI from lagging measures to leading ones, and clean claim rate is where that lands.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.hfma.org/data-and-insights/map-initiative/map-keys/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HFMA’s MAP Keys</a>, the industry-standard KPI set, define the measure as claims that pass all edits in the claims processing tool without manual intervention.</p>\n<p>HFMA’s own KPI guidance points providers toward a 98% clean claims rate, and puts net collection at 95% minimum with 97% to 99% optimal.</p>\n<p>The reason it’s displacing the traditional dashboard is timing. Net collection rate and days in A/R both tell you what already went wrong, weeks after the claim left your system. Clean claim rate tells you what is about to go wrong, while intervention is still possible.</p>\n<p>One caveat that undercuts a lot of dashboards: measure it at the payer, not the clearinghouse.</p>\n<p>A claim that clears your scrubber has passed your own edits, not the payer’s, so clearinghouse-level reporting flatters the number and hides exactly the errors you are trying to catch.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000006",
      "key": "086dc61b-c63e-4215-8be0-27938c1e4209",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "label",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What it means for you"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "If you track one number this year, track this one. It’s also the metric any automation vendor or outsourcing partner should be willing to be measured against, provided you agree on the definition first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000005",
      "key": "8291f855-51ae-4bf7-b691-98f853426648",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "number",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "03"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Prior Authorization Automation Is Accelerating on a Regulatory Clock"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "trend-3"
        },
        {
          "alias": "body",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>Prior authorization is the most expensive manual process left in the revenue cycle, and CMS has now attached a deadline to fixing it.</p>\n<p>Start with what it costs practices today. <a href=\"https://www.mgma.com/articles/the-prior-authorization-landscape-in-2025\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MGMA’s Annual Regulatory Burden Report</a> found 92% of medical groups hired or reassigned staff solely to handle prior authorization volume, 60% said at least three employees touch a single request, and 35% spend upwards of 35 minutes on average per request.</p>\n<p>That burden persists because the transaction never got automated the way the rest of the revenue cycle did.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.caqh.org/insights/caqh-index-report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2025 CAQH Index</a> puts electronic adoption of medical prior authorization at <a href=\"https://www.ajmc.com/view/caqh-index-finds-20-billion-in-cost-savings-opportunities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">40%, up from 31% in the 2023 Index</a> but still far behind claim status inquiry at 81% and claim payment at 78%.</p>\n<figure class=\"rcm-chart reveal-chart\" aria-labelledby=\"electronic-caption\">\n  <div class=\"rcm-chart-head\"><figcaption id=\"electronic-caption\"><h3>Medical transactions conducted fully electronically</h3><span class=\"rcm-chart-source\">Source: <a href=\"https://www.caqh.org/insights/caqh-index-report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2025 CAQH Index</a></span></figcaption><span class=\"rcm-chart-note\">2025 adoption</span></div>\n  <div class=\"bar-chart\">\n    <div class=\"hbar-row\"><b>Claim status inquiry</b><div class=\"hbar-track\"><div class=\"hbar-fill\" style=\"--w:81%;--c:#9cc6e9\"></div></div><em>81%</em></div>\n    <div class=\"hbar-row\"><b>Claim payment</b><div class=\"hbar-track\"><div class=\"hbar-fill\" style=\"--w:78%;--c:#9cc6e9\"></div></div><em>78%</em></div>\n    <div class=\"hbar-row\"><b>Prior authorization</b><div class=\"hbar-track\"><div class=\"hbar-fill\" style=\"--w:40%;--c:#2369a8\"></div></div><em>40%</em></div>\n  </div>\n</figure>\n<p>Closing gaps like that one across all transaction types is where CAQH finds <a href=\"https://www.ajmc.com/view/caqh-index-finds-20-billion-in-cost-savings-opportunities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">more than $20 billion in unrealized savings</a>.</p>\n<p>That’s the gap <a href=\"https://www.cms.gov/initiatives/burden-reduction/overview/interoperability/policies-regulations/cms-interoperability-prior-authorization-final-rule-cms-0057-f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CMS-0057-F, the Interoperability and Prior Authorization Final Rule</a>, is built to close. It requires impacted payers to stand up FHIR-based Prior Authorization APIs, with the core requirement landing in January 2027.</p>\n<p>It compresses decision timelines to 72 hours for expedited requests and seven calendar days for standard ones, and requires payers to publish denial reasons and annual reporting metrics.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000006",
      "key": "b8530e3e-f556-40db-81ac-66f920c0dfd9",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "label",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What it means for you"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "The payer-side infrastructure is being built whether you prepare or not. The rule covers Medicare Advantage, Medicaid and CHIP managed care, state Medicaid and CHIP FFS, and QHP issuers on the federal exchanges, so your workflow stays hybrid, and knowing which of your payers fall inside that scope is the first move."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000005",
      "key": "eb851191-f40f-47e9-b597-6f360de450e6",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "number",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "04"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Payer Automation Is Outpacing Manual Claim Work"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "trend-4"
        },
        {
          "alias": "body",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>Insurers check your claims with machines. Your staff fixes the rejections. Those two things don’t scale at the same rate.</p>\n<p>When a claim reaches a payer, it runs against thousands of rules in about a second: is this code valid alongside that one, does the diagnosis support the procedure, was authorization on file.</p>\n<p>Anything out of place bounces automatically. A human reviewer once applied judgment to borderline claims. Automated review applies the rule.</p>\n<p>Your side still runs at human speed. A rejection lands, a biller works out what went wrong, corrects it, and resubmits. One claim, one person, twenty minutes.</p>\n<p>Annual code set changes cause spikes on a schedule, and providers feel it: 68% told <a href=\"https://www.experianplc.com/newsroom/press-releases/2025/experian-health-s-3rd-annual-state-of-claims-survey-finds-denial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Experian Health</a> that submitting clean claims is harder than a year ago, and 54% said claim errors are increasing.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000006",
      "key": "ae68a502-d3d7-47a7-ac17-d0eba360b3b5",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "label",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What it means for you"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "You can’t out-staff an automated system. The only place the math works in your favor is before submission, where one process fix prevents every future instance of that error."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000005",
      "key": "f5623932-6683-4802-9489-ffc51343534d",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "number",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "05"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "The Staffing Squeeze Is Becoming Structural"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "trend-5"
        },
        {
          "alias": "body",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>Certified coders and experienced AR follow-up staff have been hard to hire and expensive to keep for years.</p>\n<p>What changed is the volume of work landing on those thinner teams, and Experian Health’s 2025 survey names staffing shortages alongside rising denials as a core provider concern.</p>\n<p>Every denial takes about the same staff time to work, so twice the denials means twice the hours. Your headcount didn’t double. That time comes out of finding the causes, so the same claims keep breaking.</p>\n<div class=\"rcm-calculator\" aria-labelledby=\"calc-title\">\n  <span class=\"rcm-section-label\">Interactive workload lens</span>\n  <h3 id=\"calc-title\">See what denial rework costs in staff time</h3>\n  <p>Illustrative estimate based on the article’s 20-minute manual rework example.</p>\n  <div class=\"calc-controls\">\n    <div class=\"calc-field\"><label for=\"claims\">Monthly claims <output id=\"claims-out\">2,000</output></label><input id=\"claims\" type=\"range\" min=\"500\" max=\"10000\" step=\"500\" value=\"2000\"></div>\n    <div class=\"calc-field\"><label for=\"rate\">Denial rate <output id=\"rate-out\">10%</output></label><input id=\"rate\" type=\"range\" min=\"5\" max=\"20\" step=\"1\" value=\"10\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"calc-result\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n    <div><strong id=\"denials-out\">200</strong><span>denied claims per month</span></div>\n    <div><strong id=\"hours-out\">67</strong><span>rework hours per month</span></div>\n    <div><strong id=\"days-out\">8.3</strong><span>eight-hour workdays</span></div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000006",
      "key": "139a3737-b458-4cad-8320-7408ad62ca9e",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "label",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What it means for you"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "You won’t hire your way out of this. Coders are scarce, and denials are growing faster than payroll, which leaves two levers: automate the repetitive work, or add capacity through a partner. Most practices end up using both."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000005",
      "key": "0e12f27d-6d2f-49d0-b13d-645a51c1b9e7",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "number",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "06"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "The AI ROI Gap Is Finally Being Named Out Loud"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "trend-6"
        },
        {
          "alias": "body",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>For two years, the industry talked about AI adoption. In 2026, it’s talking about returns, and the numbers are uncomfortable.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.hfma.org/technology/most-healthcare-organizations-are-adopting-ai-in-the-revenue-cycle-hfma-poll/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HFMA and FinThrive research</a> found 63% of healthcare organizations had integrated AI-powered automation into claims processing, but only 15% reported clear positive ROI.</p>\n<p>Experian Health’s State of Claims research found 67% of finance professionals believe AI can improve claims processes while only 14% had applied it to denials.</p>\n<p>A <a href=\"https://www.hfma.org/revenue-cycle/denials-management/ai-adoption-in-denials-management-lags-as-other-rcm-uses-expand/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2025 Bain survey</a> has also put denials-specific AI adoption at roughly one in five providers, well behind documentation support and coding.</p>\n<figure class=\"rcm-chart reveal-chart\" aria-labelledby=\"gap-caption\">\n  <div class=\"rcm-chart-head\"><figcaption id=\"gap-caption\"><h3>The distance between confidence and proven use</h3><span class=\"rcm-chart-source\">Sources: HFMA and FinThrive (top); Experian Health State of Claims (bottom)</span></figcaption><span class=\"rcm-chart-note\">Percentage points</span></div>\n  <div class=\"gap-chart\">\n    <div class=\"gap-row\"><span class=\"gap-label\">Integrated AI into claims processing vs. clear positive ROI</span><div class=\"gap-line\" style=\"--from:15%;--to:63%;--mid:39%\"><span class=\"gap-value from\">15%</span><span class=\"gap-value to\">63%</span><span class=\"gap-points\">48-point gap</span></div></div>\n    <div class=\"gap-row\"><span class=\"gap-label\">Applied AI to denials vs. believe AI can improve claims</span><div class=\"gap-line\" style=\"--from:14%;--to:67%;--mid:40.5%\"><span class=\"gap-value from\">14%</span><span class=\"gap-value to\">67%</span><span class=\"gap-points\">53-point gap</span></div></div>\n  </div>\n</figure>\n<p>These numbers show us that adoption is broad, and that returns are concentrated in just a small minority. The highest-value use case is the least automated.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000006",
      "key": "d2aab2d5-e32e-489e-96be-4193d2c8b708",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "label",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What it means for you"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Before you sign anything, write down the number the tool is supposed to move and what it reads today. Clean claim rate, denial rate on one payer, hours spent on eligibility checks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000005",
      "key": "4388b04f-deab-4258-ba64-b0c19009ca8e",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "number",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "07"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Outsourcing Is Shifting From a Cost Play to a Capacity Play"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "trend-7"
        },
        {
          "alias": "body",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>Outsourcing used to be evaluated mainly on cost. In 2026, practices are reaching for it because they can’t hire fast enough, and a partner comes with coders and AR staff already trained.</p>\n<p>The work that moves out is usually the repetitive, high-volume kind: eligibility checks, prior authorization follow-up, coding, charge entry, payment posting, AR follow-up, and appeals.</p>\n<p>What has changed is what practices ask before signing. Instead of leading with price, they ask what the partner measures, whether denial patterns get reported back so the front desk can fix them, and how patient data is protected.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000006",
      "key": "a0cedc94-14e8-40ab-8f62-925f273a2389",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "label",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What it means for you"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Add up what billing really costs you now. Salaries, benefits, training, software, the weeks a seat sits empty, and the denials nobody had time to work. That total is the number to compare a partner against, not the salary line by itself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000004",
      "key": "144d49e2-baa1-4c59-8a3b-cbd250939d93",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "heading",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Questions Revenue Cycle Leaders Are Asking"
        },
        {
          "alias": "level",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[\"h2\"]"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorId",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "faq"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000007",
      "key": "da8fa839-415f-42e1-9e0c-6c4e1b41c38f",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "question",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Why are claim denials increasing?"
        },
        {
          "alias": "answer",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Payers now screen claims automatically, prior authorization rules are enforced more strictly, and annual code updates create fresh mismatches. Most of the increase isn’t sloppy billing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000007",
      "key": "be4bf78f-a332-4910-b93a-79f0cb9a3e73",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "question",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "What is the average denial rate for physician practices?"
        },
        {
          "alias": "answer",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "HFMA puts the industry average at 5% to 10%, with under 5% optimal. Experian Health found 41% of providers are above 10%. Behavioral health, orthopedics, and physical therapy run higher than primary care."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000007",
      "key": "125988d0-1f76-444d-8899-3dbf7764fa41",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "question",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "How can you reduce denials without hiring more staff?"
        },
        {
          "alias": "answer",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Move the work upstream. Verify eligibility at registration, tie authorization tracking to scheduling, and fix the workflow behind your top denial codes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000007",
      "key": "7096642d-6eeb-449e-8d30-a2af7ee1cce3",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "question",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Is AI worth it for medical billing?"
        },
        {
          "alias": "answer",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "It depends on scope. Broad platform rollouts have a poor track record, with far more organizations adopting AI than reporting clear returns. Narrow uses like eligibility automation pay back faster."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000007",
      "key": "d773fbe3-4ad0-4302-a19d-250dda0284cf",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "question",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "How much does RCM outsourcing cost per claim?"
        },
        {
          "alias": "answer",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Usually a percentage of collections or a flat rate per claim, depending on specialty and scope. Compare it against what billing costs you today, including benefits, software, and vacant seats."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000008",
      "key": "7dfe0132-f862-471c-aa30-820fc2197c44",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "eyebrow",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Revenue cycle assessment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Ready to See Where Your Revenue Cycle Is Leaking?"
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<p>Most practices know they are collecting less than they should. Knowing why is harder. The denial rate creeps up, the same codes keep coming back, and nobody has a free afternoon to trace them.</p>\n<p>That’s the work Centro does. We handle eligibility verification, prior authorization follow-up, coding, charge capture, payment posting, AR follow-up, and appeals.</p>\n<div class=\"rcm-services\" aria-label=\"Centro revenue cycle services\">\n  <span>Eligibility verification</span><span>Prior authorization follow-up</span><span>Medical coding</span><span>Charge capture</span><span>Payment posting</span><span>AR follow-up and appeals</span>\n</div>\n<p>Because we work within your EHR and deal directly with insurers, denials come back to you with the cause attached and the upstream fix identified.</p>\n<p>Centro has run healthcare revenue cycle operations since 2009, across five delivery countries. We stay deliberately boutique, so you keep the same team rather than a rotating account manager, and every engagement is HIPAA compliant.</p>"
        },
        {
          "alias": "buttonLabel",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Contact Centro"
        },
        {
          "alias": "buttonLink",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "[{\"name\":\"Contact Centro\",\"url\":\"https://centrocdx.com/get-in-touch/\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"queryString\":null}]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a7010006-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-000000000002",
      "key": "2cadbeba-c448-4a73-bfbc-d8122f3cf7e4",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "<div class=\"rcm-disclaimer\">\n  <p><em>Centro is a healthcare business process outsourcing and revenue cycle management company supporting physician practices, clinics, and hospitals across the United States.</em></p>\n  <p><em>Centro’s services cover the full revenue cycle from patient access and eligibility verification through medical coding, claims submission, denial management, and accounts receivable follow-up.</em></p>\n</div>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
